  "generated_text": "1. **Express $27\\sqrt{3}$ as a power of 3:**\n   \\[\n   27\\sqrt{3} = 3^3 \\cdot 3^{1/2} = 3^{3 + 1/2} = 3^{7/2}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Apply the logarithm:**\n   \\[\n   \\log_3 27\\sqrt{3} = \\log_3 3^{7/2}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Use the logarithm property:**\n   \\[\n   \\log_3 3^{7/2} = \\frac{7}{2} \\cdot \\log_3 3\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify:**\n   \\[\n   \\log_3 3 = 1\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   \\log_3 27\\sqrt{3} = \\frac{7}{2} \\cdot 1 = \\frac{7}{2}\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}}\n\\]",
